Inclusion Criteria:

1. Female;
2. Aged 18-70 years;
3. Preoperative pathologically confirmed diagnosis of breast cancer, treated at Sir Run Run Shaw Hospital, Zhejiang University School of Medicine (lead center) or other participating centers;
4. Voluntary participation in the study with signed informed consent;
5. Desire for breast conservation;
6. Clinical stage I-II early breast cancer: tumor size T1-T2, with adequate breast volume and an appropriate tumor-to-breast volume ratio, such that a satisfactory breast shape can be maintained after surgery;
7. Selected patients with clinical stage III disease (except inflammatory breast cancer) who meet the criteria for breast-conserving surgery after downstaging by preoperative therapy may be carefully considered;
