* unstable psychiatric illness, such as psychosis or major depression;
* severe disability with Expanded Disability Status Scale (EDSS) score \> 7.5;
* severe cognitive impairment that would not enable PwMS to answer to questionnaires correctly (i.e. dementia), according to the patient's medical records.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Clinical diagnosis of Open-Angle Glaucoma or Ocular Hypertension for at least 6 months;
* Other protocol-defined inclusion criteria may apply.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Prior angle surgery in the study eye, severe visual field loss in either eye;
* Other protocol-defined exclusion criteria may apply.

Inclusion Criteria:

* age over 18;
* female participants only;

Exclusion Criteria:

* with congenital heart disease or with other family disease history
* participants receiving hormone therapy

Inclusion Criteria:

* Age 18 and above, male or female
* Conform to the diagnostic criteria of immune Thrombocytopenia (ITP)
* Diagnosis of ITP ≥3 months, and with a platelet count of \ 3 months；More than 6 months after splenectomy.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Subjects with primary disease of important organs (liver, kidney, heart, etc.), or with immune system diseases;
* Secondary thrombocytopenia caused by various reasons, such as connective tissue disorders, bone marrow hematopoietic failure disease, myelodysplastic syndrome, malignancy, drugs, inherited thrombocytopenia, common variable immune deficiency, lymphoma, etc.;
* Subjects infected with human immunodeficiency virus (HIV);
