1. Renal: Serum creatinine ≤ 1.5 × ULN or creatinine clearance ≥ 50 mL/min \[Cockcroft-Gault formula: (\[140 - age\] × weight \[kg\] × \[0.85 for females only\]) / (72 × creatinine (mg/dl))\]; qualitative urine protein ≤ 1+; if qualitative urine protein ≥ 2+, a 24-hour urine protein quantification test is required, and a result of \ 1.5 × 10⁹/L; hemoglobin level ≥ 90 g/L; platelet count ≥ 90 × 10⁹/L (administration of medications with leukocyte/platelet-boosting effects within 14 days prior to enrollment to meet eligibility criteria is not permitted).
